Hi Chris,

One option is to use nimble's capability to call an R function, even during compiled execution.  This is described in section 10.7 of the user manual.  It won't be as fast as having a compiled version, but it will work.  Let us know if you get stuck making that work.

Another option would be to look into R's source code in C for digamma, where digamma calls dpsifn <https://github.com/wch/r-source/blob/af7f52f70101960861e5d995d3a4bec010bc89e6/src/nmath/polygamma.c>.  Since it is open source, I think you can copy and use it as long as you follow the licensing.

-Perry

