I'm now getting "inconsistent dimensionality" for the variable I need to create using the digamma function. I'd appreciate any help that can be offered here. I'm trying to compare two Poisson time-series models. To make the comparison fair, I'm trying to write a previously published psuedo-Bayesian model called PEWMA (Poisson Exponentially Weighted Moving Average) in Nimble to make it "fully" Bayesian like the other model, which itself it written in Nimble. I'm struggling a bit to get it working, partly because it's a bit difficult to convert the original authors' notation and r-code into a Nimble model, and partly because I need this "digamma" function. Here's the model as it stands—I'm using the "devel" version of Nimble compiled and installed this morning:

poisTSCode <- nimbleCode({
   omega ~ dunif(0,1)
   alpha0 ~ dunif(0,100)
   beta0 ~ dunif(0,100)
   alpha[1] <- omega * alpha0 + Y[1]
   rho[1] <- nimDigamma(alpha0) - nimDigamma(omega * alpha0)
   if(K > 1){
      A[1:K,1:K] <- inverse(diag(x=rep(1000,K)))
      mB[1:K] <- rep(0,K)
      B[1:K] ~ dmnorm(mean=mB[1:K], prec=A[1:K,1:K])
      lreg[1] <- exp(inprod(X[1,1:K], B[1:K])) * exp(rho[1])
      beta[1] <- omega * beta0 + lreg[1]
   }else{
      B ~ dnorm(mean=0,sd=1000)
      lreg[1] <- exp(X[1] * B) * exp(rho[1])
      beta[1] <- omega * beta0 + lreg[1]
   }
   mu_star[1] ~ dgamma(alpha0,beta0)
   mu[1] <- mu_star[1] * lreg[1]
   Y[1] ~ dpois(mu[1])
   for (j in 2:T){
      rho[j] <- nimDigamma(alpha[j-1]) - nimDigamma(omega * alpha[j-1])
      alpha[j] <- omega * alpha[j-1] + Y[j]
      if(K > 1){
         lreg[j] <- exp(inprod(X[j,1:K], B[1:K])) * exp(rho[j])
         beta[j] <- omega * beta[j-1] + lreg[j]
      }else{
         lreg[j] <- exp(X[j] * B) * exp(rho[j])
         beta[j] <- omega * beta[j-1] + lreg[j]
      }
      mu_star[j] ~ dgamma(alpha[j],beta[j])
      mu[j] <- mu_star[j] * lreg[j]
      Y[j] ~ dpois(mu[j])
   }})

Here's the nimbleFunction again that approximates digamma:

nimDigamma <- nimbleFunction(

   run = function(X = double(1)){

      t_ <- seq(1e-7,max(X)+10,0.001)

      output <- c()
      for(x in X){

         di_y <- sum( ( (exp(-t_)/t_) - (exp(-x * t_) / (1 - exp(-t_))) ) * 0.001 )

         output <- c(output, di_y)
      }
      returnType(double(1))
      return(output)
   }
)

Here's the current error I'm getting when I try to run the model (see attached for the full R script for the Nimble model and an R data object containing the test data):

defining model...
Error in addMissingIndexingRecurse(code[[i]], dimensionsList) :
  inconsistent dimensionality provided for node 'rho'

I assume that I've done something wrong regarding scalars and vectors maybe? I've also tried changing the variable declarations in the nimDigamma function to double() and double(0) with the same result.

Any ideas would be much appreciated.

Thanks again!

C

