Hi Chris,

Below is an example that works.

I think the problem is that the nimbleRcall only works in compiled execution, not uncompiled.  We should either fix that or provide a useful error-trap.

Perry
-------

library(nimble)

Rdigamma <- nimbleRcall(function(x = double()){}, Rfun = 'digamma',
                        returnType = double())

code <- nimbleCode({
    b ~ dexp(1)
    a <- Rdigamma(b)
})

model <- nimbleModel(code, calculate = FALSE)

cmodel <- compileNimble(model)

cmodel$simulate()
cmodel$b
cmodel$a
digamma(cmodel$b)

