Dear Nimble Team,

I'm trying to truncate an interval to define a random effect:

………

  sigma.alpha ~ dunif(0,10)

  tau.alpha <- pow(sigma2.alpha, -2)

  sigma2.alpha <- pow(sigma.alpha, 2)

  for (i in 1:M){

    for(t in 1:T){

      ep.alpha[i,t] ~ T(dnorm(0, tau.alpha),-15,15)

      logit(lam0[i,t])<-mu.alpha[t] + ep.alpha[i,t]

    }

……………

But when I compiled, I got:

defining model...

building model...

setting data and initial values...

running calculate on model (any error reports that follow may simply reflect missing values in model variables) ... Error in if (-15 <= model$ep.alpha[getNodeFunctionIndexedInfo(INDEXEDNODEINFO_,  :

  valor ausente donde TRUE/FALSE es necesario # (sorry, in Spanish…)

checking model sizes and dimensions... This model is not fully initialized. This is not an error. To see which variables are not initialized, use model$initializeInfo(). For more information on model initialization, see help(modelInitialization).

model building finished.

What’s wrong in the code?

Thank you,

José

