Hi José,

Actually, there is nothing wrong. All that happened is that your code failed to initialize, and in this case that manifested itself with an error reported from R.  However the model-building then proceeded and finished.

You can use "calculate = FALSE" to avoid having nimbleModel try to initialize (including calculations) the entire model, which will avoid the error message (and often run faster).

Perry

